From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: marty <marty@fyai.co.nz>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 19:51:53 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] RetroPlayer: make the GL context current before the client
 runs

mupen64plus-nx with its GLideN64 plugin segfaulted the moment it started, with a
backtrace containing none of our code: retro_run() -> GLideN64 -> strstr() ->
strchr(). That is strstr(glGetString(GL_EXTENSIONS), ...) on a NULL return.

The pool created its EGL context lazily in CreateRenderBuffer(), which only runs
when the client first asks for a framebuffer. But a client sets its renderer up
in context_reset and during its first retro_run, before it asks for anything,
and reads the extension string there. No current context, NULL, segfault inside
the client.

Creating it in EnableHardwareRendering() instead puts it on the right thread:
that is reached from the client's own SET_HW_RENDER, and the crash log showed
OpenStream() and the faulting retro_run() on the same thread.

This is the ordering Kodi's OpenGL_Roadmap.md warns about under "GL Context
Management" - contexts are thread-specific and rendering has to happen on the
thread that owns one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../buffers/RenderBufferPoolFBO.cpp           | 25 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/RetroPlayer/buffers/RenderBufferPoolFBO.cpp b/xbmc/cores/RetroPlayer/buffers/RenderBufferPoolFBO.cpp
index 781ff56..106f85a 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/RetroPlayer/buffers/RenderBufferPoolFBO.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/RetroPlayer/buffers/RenderBufferPoolFBO.cpp
@@ -36,6 +36,31 @@ void CRenderBufferPoolFBO::EnableHardwareRendering(bool depth, bool stencil)
 {
   m_depth = depth;
   m_stencil = stencil;
+
+  // The context has to be current on this thread *now*, not lazily on the first
+  // GetBuffer(). A client sets up its renderer in context_reset and during its
+  // first retro_run, before it ever asks for a framebuffer, and the first thing
+  // it does there is read glGetString(GL_EXTENSIONS). With no current context
+  // that returns NULL and the client segfaults inside its own strstr() - which
+  // is what mupen64plus-nx did here, with a backtrace containing none of our
+  // code.
+  //
+  // This runs on the same thread as the game loop: CGameClientStreams::
+  // EnableHardwareRendering() is reached from the client's SET_HW_RENDER, and
+  // the crash log showed OpenStream() and the faulting retro_run() on one
+  // thread.
+  if (m_eglContext == EGL_NO_CONTEXT && !CreateContext())
+  {
+    CLog::Log(LOGERROR, "RetroPlayer[RENDER]: Cannot enable hardware rendering, no GL context");
+    return;
+  }
+
+  if (m_fboId == 0 && !CreateFramebuffer())
+  {
+    CLog::Log(LOGERROR, "RetroPlayer[RENDER]: Cannot enable hardware rendering, no framebuffer");
+    return;
+  }
+
   m_active = true;
 }
 
